# Welcome to February 27, 2026

The Singularity just closed its Series G and opened its conscience.

OpenAI raised [$110 billion in new funding](https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/27/openai-raises-110b-in-one-of-the-largest-private-funding-rounds-in-history/) at a $730 billion pre-money valuation — one of the largest private rounds in history — with Amazon contributing [$50 billion](https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/aws/amazon-open-ai-strategic-partnership-investment), and Nvidia and SoftBank at [$30 billion each](https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/amazon-invest-50-billion-openai-2026-02-27/). The Amazon deal is not charity: OpenAI commits to consuming [2 gigawatts of Trainium capacity](https://openai.com/index/amazon-partnership/) through AWS, making Amazon the exclusive third-party cloud provider for OpenAI Frontier, the company's enterprise agent platform. OpenAI and Amazon will [co-develop custom models](https://seekingalpha.com/pr/20417457-openai-and-amazon-announce-strategic-partnership) to power Amazon's consumer applications. The company that started as a nonprofit research lab is now worth more than Boeing, Coca-Cola, and Bank of America combined — and its chip supplier just [invested $30 billion](https://seekingalpha.com/news/4558700-openai-confirms-110b-funding-round-with-50b-from-amazon-and-30b-from-nvidia-softbank) while simultaneously selling it the chips.

**The company that drew the red line is holding it — barely.** Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei told the Pentagon ["we cannot in good conscience accede to their request"](https://apnews.com/article/anthropic-pentagon-ai-hegseth-dario-amodei-b72d1894bc842d9acf026df3867bee8a) as the Friday 5:01 PM deadline arrived, rejecting contract language that would allow Claude's use for [mass domestic surveillance and fully autonomous weapons](https://www.reuters.com/technology/pentagon-anthropic-feud-has-sales-ai-warfare-stake-friday-deadline-looms-2026-02-27/). U.S. senators [urged the Pentagon to withdraw](https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/us-senators-make-two-demands-as-anthropic-ceo-dario-amodei-says-no-to-pentagon/articleshow/128854311.cms) its ultimatum, arguing Congress should set the rules for military AI. But earlier this week, Anthropic quietly [dropped its flagship safety pledge](https://time.com/7380854/exclusive-anthropic-drops-flagship-safety-pledge/) — the commitment to halt model training if safety measures couldn't keep pace with capabilities — replacing hard pause triggers with [discretionary, competition-aware guidelines](https://www.technobezz.com/news/anthropic-revises-safety-policy-to-allow-ai-development-despite-unmitigated-risks). The company will stand its ground on weapons but [no longer promises to stop building](https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/25/tech/anthropic-safety-policy-change) if what it builds outpaces its own understanding.

**The intelligence economy is eating its host.** IDC projects [a 12.9% collapse in global smartphone shipments](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-02-26/idc-sees-13-collapse-in-smartphone-market-due-to-memory-crisis) for 2026 — the steepest annual contraction ever recorded — as wafer capacity [floods toward AI DRAM and enterprise NAND](https://www.moneycontrol.com/technology/global-smartphone-shipments-set-for-record-12-4-drop-in-2026-as-memory-crunch-bites-article-13845706.html), tripling mobile memory prices since Q3 2025. Average smartphone prices will hit a [record $523](https://opentools.ai/news/memory-chip-shortage-sparks-unprecedented-dip-in-smartphone-shipments), up 14%, with mid-range brands like Xiaomi and Oppo [slashing shipment targets by 20%](https://www.pcmag.com/news/smartphone-makers-brace-for-largest-decline-ever-amid-memory-crunch). The machines that think are starving the machines that scroll.

**The layoff wave has a spokesperson.** Jack Dorsey cut [over 4,000 Block employees](https://venturebeat.com/orchestration/jack-dorseys-block-cuts-40-of-staff-4-000-people-and-yes-its-because-of-ai) — nearly half the company — to pivot toward an ["intelligence-native" future](https://www.newsweek.com/read-jack-dorseys-full-statement-block-layoffs-11590862), despite Block posting [$2.87 billion in gross profit](https://www.sfgate.com/tech/article/jack-dorsey-block-layoffs-21944033.php), up 24% year-over-year. Dorsey warned that other companies [will follow "within the next year."](https://www.sfgate.com/tech/article/jack-dorsey-block-layoffs-21944033.php) Goldman Sachs economists estimate AI is already responsible for [5,000 to 10,000 monthly net job losses](https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/goldman-sachs-warns-ai-fueled-layoffs-could-raise-the-unemployment-rate-this-year-chart-154251740.html) in exposed industries, and project unemployment could rise to [4.5% by year-end](https://www.newsbreak.com/the-daily-overview-358953826/4511492910616-goldman-sachs-warns-ai-layoffs-could-spike-the-jobless-rate-in-2026). Block's stock [surged on the news](https://www.investing.com/news/economy-news/jack-dorseys-block-to-cut-over-4000-jobs-as-ai-use-expands-shares-surge-4529839). The market rewards the cut.

**Nvidia is selling shovels to everyone simultaneously.** The stock [dropped another 2.4%](https://fool.com/coverage/stock-market-today/2026/02/26/stock-market-today-feb-26-nvidia-falls-after-record-results-fail-to-ease-ai-bubble-concerns/) on Friday after Wednesday's 5.5% post-earnings plunge wiped [$260 billion in a single session](https://www.reuters.com/business/global-markets-trading-day-graphic-2026-02-26/) — this despite record $68.1 billion in Q4 revenue, a [73% year-over-year surge](https://www.hartware.de/2026/02/27/nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-fourth-quarter-and-fiscal-2026/), and a Q1 guide of $78 billion that [crushed consensus by $5.4 billion](https://blockonomi.com/nvidia-stock-slides-5-after-strong-q4-earnings-beat/). Jensen Huang announced the [Rubin platform](http://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/meta-builds-ai-infrastructure-with-nvidia) — a 10x reduction in inference cost over Blackwell — and a multi-year partnership with Meta to deploy [millions of Blackwell and Rubin GPUs](https://www.techpowerup.com/346493/meta-partners-with-nvidia-to-deploy-millions-of-blackwell-and-rubin-gpus). Goldman Sachs projects hyperscaler AI capex will reach [$667 billion in 2026](https://news.futunn.com/en/post/69261531/goldman-sachs-on-ai-trading-ai-infrastructure-faces-risks-in), up 62% year-over-year. The infrastructure buildout has never been larger and the market has never been less sure it will pay off.

**The consolidation wave has reached Hollywood.** Paramount Skydance is [poised to acquire Warner Bros. Discovery](https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/netflix-declines-raise-bid-warner-bros-discovery-1236674149/) after Netflix bowed out Thursday, declaring the deal ["no longer financially attractive"](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/02/26/warner-bros-discovery-paramount-skydance-deal-superior-netflix.html). David Ellison is building a media empire with [dozens of TV channels, multiple studios, and two newsrooms](https://www.channel3000.com/news/national-and-world-news/paramount-emerges-victorious-over-netflix-in-warner-bros-discovery-bidding-war/article_072aa447-6b80-5433-bc63-a1c0065599e1.html) — the old economy consolidating as fast as the new one can hollow it out. Meanwhile, SpaceX launched [its 30th Starlink mission of the year](https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/02/27/live-coverage-spacex-planning-pre-dawn-falcon-9-launch-from-cape-canaveral-of-29-starlink-satellites/) from Cape Canaveral Friday morning, and Trump [directed the Pentagon to release government files on UFOs](https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-orders-agencies-identify-release-government-files-aliens-2026-02-20/), though Hegseth's own staff is reportedly [pushing back on full declassification](https://www.ibtimes.co.uk/trump-ufo-disclosure-pentagon-resistance-1781453) over fears the phenomenon may have "demonic" or "interdimensional" implications.

The company that won't build weapons dropped the pledge to stop building, the company that builds everything just raised $110 billion from its own customers, and the market punished the record and rewarded the layoff — but at least the Pentagon is worried about demons.
